  "texto": "Feed post\n\nY Combinator\n\n2mo • \n\nPloy turns your website into your company's growth engine.\n\nMost founders ship a website when they start a company, then struggle to leverage it for growth.\n\nPloy is an all-in-one marketing platform that runs your website and growth channels end-to-end. It recreates your brand from your existing site or builds one from scratch. Then Ploy gets to work: spin up personalized pages, run an SEO audit, de-anonymize your traffic, or launch paid ads in minutes.\n\nPloy is founded by Bryant Chou, former co-founder and CTO of Webflow (S13). After spending the last decade-plus building the infrastructure behind millions of websites and building the GTM machine behind it, Bryant is taking his vision for the web one step further: not just helping companies build websites, but helping websites work for them.\n\nThe website is just the beginning. Drop in your URL to watch Ploy get to work: https://lnkd.in/gS6VcvcU\n\n1,196 reactions\n1,196\n\n74 comments\n74 comments\n\n•\n\n29 reposts\n29 reposts\n\nLike\nComment\nRepost\nSend\n\nMost relevant\n\nConnor J. Wilson, Hiring Premium Profile 3rd+\nConnor J. Wilson \n • 3rd+\n\n🧭 Founder @ Pilot, Multiplayer Consumer AI for Travel (120K travelers, $2.2mil raised) | exited NiceJob ($30mil bootstrapped)\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nBryant Chou we're webflow customers and used to love it, but it's slow and dated now. We'd planned to build our next iteration with Claude Code and then self-host instead. What would you say is the biggest reason we should use Ploy instead?\n\n4 reactions\n4\n\n1\n1\n\nBryant Chou Premium Profile 2nd\nBryant Chou \n • 2nd\n\njust ployin around here\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nConnor J. Wilson Webflow is great if you have the team to help you \n\nI would use ploy if you care about design consistency so all of your buttons are the same and not hallucinated variants\n\nI would use ploy if you want to ensure your site actually is built for scaling content engines that rank and are cited\n\nI would use ploy if you want growth strategies that run on autopilot for you across web, ads, email, sales operations - the entire GTM front office is what ploy can accelerate and bring you more customers in less time\n… more\n\n2 reactions\n2\n\nMichael McCarty 3rd+\nMichael McCarty • 3rd+\n\nChief Product Officer @ Retired.com\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nThis is becoming a trend now. I just tried frontpage.host yesterday which seems similar to this. How do they intend to differentiate from Frontpage? \n\n5 reactions\n5\n\n3\n3\n\nSee previous replies\n\nRishi Khiani Premium Profile 3rd+\nRishi Khiani \n • 3rd+\n\nBuilding Craise & Kaam.com · Founder, Antfarm · Fork Media · previously Scootsy, Times Internet (CEO), Network18\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nMarcus Schack I agree \n\n0 \n\nHussain Ahmed Tusar 3rd+\nHussain Ahmed Tusar • 3rd+\n\nWe help SaaS founders turn raw footage into content that builds trust and drives subscribers\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nWhat stands out to me is the evolution of the website itself. For years, websites have mostly been treated as digital brochures: build it, publish it, and hope visitors convert. But growth today requires constant iteration across SEO, personalization, attribution, and acquisition. Ploy feels like a step toward making the website an active participant in the GTM engine rather than a passive destination. Given your experience building the infrastructure behind millions of websites at Webflow, you're uniquely positioned to rethink what the next generation of company websites should look like. Excited to see where you take this. 🙂‍↕️\n\nBryant Chou\n… more\n\n2 reactions\n2\n\nObi E. Verified Profile 3rd+\nObi E. \n • 3rd+\n\nFounder/CEO @ HM2U | Connecting Nigeria to UK, USA & Canada🛒 Marketplace: ⁠HomeMarket2U📦 Cargo: HM2U Logistics💼 Talent: HM2U HireEngineering secure tech solutions for global diaspora trade.\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nThis is an interesting evolution of the company website—from a digital brochure to an active growth engine. The real opportunity is helping founders bridge the gap between building a product and building a repeatable customer acquisition system.\nThe best websites don't just attract visitors—they generate customers. Turning websites into autonomous growth engines is a compelling vision.\n… more\n\n1 reaction\n1\n\nPratham Jangra Premium Profile 3rd+\nPratham Jangra \n • 3rd+\n\nResearcher @CCI | Ex-SDE @Expedia Group | Full-stack Dev\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nJust curious, how would ploy help a business like of welding electrodes? In what particular ways would it change their website for a complete makeover and business boost or business reach?\n\n1 reaction\n1\n\n1\n1\n\nChase Binnie Verified Profile 3rd+\nChase Binnie \n • 3rd+\n\nCEO of RetailWire - daily briefing to 20,000+ retail industry leaders. Roundtable host and speaker. Superconnector for retailers, tech, and capital | Bentonville, AR\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nPratham Jangra I'd work on building the network of partners, distributors, etc\n\n1 reaction\n1\n\nInsightful Technologies Verified\nInsightful Technologies \n\n4,494 followers\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nY Combinator\nTurning a website into an active growth engine instead of just a digital storefront is an exciting evolution. Which AI-powered marketing capability do you think will create the biggest impact for businesses personalization, SEO automation, or intelligent lead generation?\n\n0 \n\nVraify \nVraify\n\n496 followers\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nExciting launch! Automating growth and content synthesis end-to-end is a massive step forward. At the frontier of model development, we are seeing that the performance of specialized marketing and personalization agents is heavily dependent on high-fidelity, domain-aligned alignment data. Platforms like Ploy show what happens when you combine elite UX with robust underlying models. Congrats to Bryant Chou and the team!\n… more\n\n0 \n\nValentin Radu Premium Profile 2nd\nValentin Radu \n • 2nd\n\n↳ Omniconvert: helping DTC + retailers grow using Data + AI + Experimentation\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nThe idea sounds great. \nI’d be doing way more QA for a company that raised 27M pre-revenue and wants to build websites for others.\n\n3 reactions\n3\n\n2\n2\n\nSee previous replies\n\nJonathan M. Verified Profile 3rd+\nJonathan M. \n • 3rd+\n\nAI Memory Engineer\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nValentin Radu seems they didn't use Ploy to rebuild their landing every now and then\n\n2 reactions\n2\n\nRhythm Shahriar Premium Profile 2nd\nRhythm Shahriar \n • 2nd\n\nCo-Founder @ ZIkbod | Startup Execution, Venture Building\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nCongratulations on the launch! Just got my hands on Ploy and it is impressive. The idea that your website can run campaigns, generate landing pages, and optimize itself in the background is something growth teams have needed for a long time. Excited to see where this goes!\n\n2 reactions\n2\n\nRon Shah Verified Profile 2nd\nRon Shah \n • 2nd\n\nBuilding tools for deeper human connection\n\n2mo\n\nFollow\n\nThis is pretty great, nice competitor to Base44 (which I love), but this seems to do more for you with figuring out your overall SEO strategy. Great to see more players here! Nice work Bryant!\n\n1 reaction\n1",
